※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4642

※ An arena may be named in a function type only where it is a parameter of the
※ signature it is written in: anywhere else a type says only that what a lambda brought
※ in lasts, and `⎕heap` is the one place that says so.

let std := ⎕import("std")

fn nowhere(n: u8) → fn(u8) in b → u8:
    λ x: u8 [n] → u8 { x + n }

@[startup]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    0u6
